No, 6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area. The constraints check also shows it is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Our guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need an application unless they match the existing in material and pattern. Since this property is not in a conservation area, that rule does not apply to your address.

This is not a formal planning opinion. Before you start work, check whether any other condition applies to your property, such as an Article 4 direction or a condition attached to a previous permission. If you're unsure, the planning desk can confirm this for you. If you have a planning application reference for the property, I can look up its details too.
